{
  "schema": "odd-semiprime-degree-existence-v1",
  "namespace": "math/reviewed-results/2026-10-23-odd-semiprime-degree-existence-v1",
  "scope": {
    "decision": "ACCEPTED_FULL_DISTINCT_ODD_SEMIPRIME_DEGREE_EXISTENCE",
    "domain": "Every pair of distinct odd primes p<q, N=pq, every primitive complex Nth root zeta, original binary N-by-N mask R and D[r,c]=R[r,c] zeta^(rc).",
    "quantifiers": "There EXISTS a binary mask R with either scalar Gram D*D=dI or DD*=dI iff d is in {0,1,p,q,pq}. Necessity applies to every arbitrary qualifying R. Sufficiency is by divisor constructions, NOT every binary mask of an allowed degree.",
    "new_credit": "Only p>=7 beyond the previously accepted 3q and 5q families. Complete all prime ratios, including the former close-prime degree window. The narrower compatibility theorem is an exact dependency, not a separate new discovery.",
    "mechanism": "Original-index CRT pairing; both square Grams and exact row/column degrees. Global cycle propagation forces a q-line, one boundary cross row then contradicts total incidence by (p-2)(q-1)>0. No Cartesian, common-support, rectangular, free-phase or finite-field replacement.",
    "inverse_row": "For the original normalized complex Fourier target, invertible approximant and simultaneous every-inverse-row sparsity, within 1<=s<=N-1 the spectral-norm infimum floor sqrt(1-s/N) is sharp exactly at s=N-1,N-p,N-q. Elsewhere the infimum is strictly larger, with no new exact value or quantitative gap rate. The full mask d=N does not yield an admissible invertible s=0 witness.",
    "review_correction": "Read the unchanged original full review together with REVIEW_CLARIFICATION.md. Its opening iff summary had an incorrect literal arbitrary-mask quantifier; the explicit clarification corrects it without changing sealed bytes or the author theorem.",
    "preserved": "The accepted prior source results and p=11,q=23 rectangular Fano obstruction retain their exact scopes. Classical two-prime cancellation gets no new credit.",
    "limits": "Not full support classification, general composite-degree necessity, exact nonsharp optima, optimal gap rates, sparse-column/commutator completion, paid construction/runtime/FFT result, historical novelty clearance or owner closure. M-SPARSE-DEFECT remains TO RESEARCH priority42; no priority/status/discovery-count changes.",
    "bounded_attribution": "Divisor-only Fourier Hadamard-submatrix cardinalities/common-support spectral sets and two-prime cancellation are known branches. Inspected statements do not supply the additional arbitrary-mask reduction; no global nonimplication or historical novelty clearance. BGH direct PDF unavailable; indexed theorem/journal mirror only, not complete PDF read."
  },
